==English==

===Etymology===
From [[needle]] + [[in]] + a + [[haystack]].

===Alternative spellings===
*[[needle-in-a-haystack]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{idiom}} Something that is [[difficult]] or [[impossible]] to locate; something impossibly [[complex]] or [[intractable]].
#:''You'll never find the paper you need on her desk.  You're looking for a '''needle in a haystack'''.''

